# Gray Part Mixing & Anti-Fingerprint Review

> **Read `apple_moderation_hardening.mdc` first.** That file is the
> authoritative source on which markers Apple's static analyzer actually
> matches; this file is the diversification checklist. Where the two
> disagree, the hardening rule wins.

The #1 reason a portfolio of gray-flow apps dies is **cross-binary similarity**:
Apple/Google cluster apps by shared code, strings and infrastructure (Guideline
4.3 Spam, sometimes account ban). Renaming public classes is NOT enough — static
analysis reads private symbols, string literals and machine code. Every new app
must differ at the level below.

**Cosmetic vs structural.** Rotating the cipher salt, the class names, the
icon set and the SharedPreferences prefix is *cosmetic* diversification — it
prevents naive string-grep matching but does not move the binary out of the
Apple cluster. Structural diversification (§6) is what actually decouples
apps. Ship both.

## 1. MUST be unique per app (never copy 1:1)

- **Cipher algorithm** (`helpers/cipher.dart`): change the *algorithm*, not just
  the seed. Rotate between families across the portfolio: FNV+LCG, RC4-style
  KSA/PRGA, table permutation, position-keyed XOR. Different algorithm = different
  machine code. Re-run `tool/encode_era_values.dart` (kept in sync) to regenerate all
  byte arrays.
- **JS injections** (WebView page): rewrite the bodies — different function names,
  variable names, control structure, string formatting, sentinel flags
  (`window.__dgaSa` → `root.dvInsetGuard`). Remove site-specific selectors like
  `.gameview-mobile-header`. These strings are grep-able; identical JS = instant cluster.
- **Network probe host** (`net_probe`): not always `cloudflare.com`. Rotate
  `apple.com` / `google.com` / own host; vary single-host vs multi-host loop.
- **User-Agent fallback** (`masked_agent`): different model/build/OS strings and
  Chrome/Safari build numbers per app.
- **Class / method / variable names** AND the **control-flow** where feasible.
- **SharedPrefs / SecureStorage key prefix** (`era.hatch.*` → `dga.*` → ...), notification
  channel id, SceneDelegate UserDefaults key.
- **pbxproj UUIDs for the NSE**: random 24-hex (`secrets.token_hex(12).upper()`),
  never a predictable pattern like `AA000001...` / `BB2026...`. Vary section order.
- **Dependency versions**: let `flutter pub add` pick latest (ranged `^`), don't
  pin the same exact versions as siblings.
- **Backend infrastructure**: different config domain / host / IP subnet per app.
  One config endpoint shared across the portfolio = trivial cluster.

## 2. Logging — nothing in release

- Dart: use an `assert`-wrapped logger so closures AND their string literals are
  stripped from release builds:
  ```dart
  void hubLog(String Function() build) {
    assert(() { debugPrint(build()); return true; }());
  }
  // call: hubLog(() => '[tag] msg $x');
  ```
  Never call bare `debugPrint('[tag] ...')` — the literal ships in release and is grep-able.
- Swift (SceneDelegate / AppDelegate): wrap every `NSLog` in `#if DEBUG ... #endif`.
- Tags themselves must be app-specific (`[DGA.*]` not shared `[ERA.*]`).

## 3. Permissions — only what the VISIBLE app justifies

The reviewer sees the white game, not the WebView. A puzzle that requests camera,
mic, photos and background fetch is a red flag.

- Remove what the game can't justify: **microphone**, background **`fetch`**.
- Keep `remote-notification` (push is a real feature).
- If a permission must stay for the WebView (camera can't be cleanly disabled
  without crashing on a camera `<input>`; photo upload needs gallery), **add a real
  white-part feature that uses it** so the reviewer sees a legitimate use — e.g. an
  avatar/profile photo picker (`image_picker`, camera + gallery). Then word the
  `NS*UsageDescription` around that feature, not the WebView.
- Declare tracking (IDFA/AppsFlyer) in App Store Connect → App Privacy, or it's an
  automatic reject.

## 4. Maximize approval

- App Store metadata (screenshots, description, keywords) must describe the WHITE
  game only — never hint at the WebView.
- Reviewer note: "this is an offline puzzle game".
- `ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption=false`, NSE `SKIP_INSTALL=YES`,
  `PRODUCT_NAME="$(TARGET_NAME)"`, NSE configs with NO `baseConfigurationReference`.
- Keep the gray flow genuinely invisible to organic/unattributed installs.

## 5. Save / uniqueization checklist (run before commit)

- [ ] `dart run tool/encode_era_values.dart` → VERIFY block matches plaintext exactly
- [ ] cipher algorithm differs from every sibling app
- [ ] JS injection bodies rewritten (not just sentinel names)
- [ ] probe host + UA fallback changed
- [ ] no bare `debugPrint`/`NSLog` strings in release path
- [ ] permissions trimmed + justified by a real white feature
- [ ] pbxproj NSE UUIDs randomized (no shared pattern), no UTF-8 BOM, CRLF preserved
- [ ] dependency versions differ from siblings
- [ ] backend domain/infra distinct
- [ ] `flutter analyze` clean, then commit + push

